From c8965d375313f64e6cab1f0a2a3f0b257efc3a07 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: forge-shepherd <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 8 Jul 2026 18:02:50 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] fix(ux): resolve five cosmetic rough edges from the new-user
 journey audit
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- _issue.js: id-required subcommands (claim/show/close/…) with no id now return a
  clean 'Missing required argument <id>' + exit 6, not a fabricated-UUID quarantine
- issue-render.js/_issue.js: writes render a concise '✓ Created <id>' confirmation
  instead of raw contract JSON (still available via --json / FORGE_JSON=1)
- orientation.js: drop internal 'D21 placeholder' text from prime/orient
- fs-class.js: soften the fail-open filesystem note (no 'database corruption' alarm)
- shell-utils.js: fold allowlisted tokens into one command line on the shell path so
  Node 22 (DEP0190) no longer warns about args + shell:true (kills the init warning)

Kernel: 842a8be7 60e196f4 9c445d18 5fc13e49 ab52cf7f (epic be7ce156). All tests + lint green.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
